14:10:49 | INFO | 🤖 Target: Got it — practice 3-6pm, morning classes. That's actually a workable structure once we identify the gaps. (And I hear you on the last part — we can just leave that where it is.) Here's how I'd map her day: **Morning (before class / between classes)** - If she has any gap between classes, that's prime real estate — quiet, undistracted, before physical fatigue sets in - Even 30 min before first class for reviewing notes or a quick reading assignment adds up over a week **Midday (after classes end, before practice — say 12-2:30pm)** - This is likely her biggest usable block. Protect it like a class itself. - Best used for: harder subjects, writing assignments, anything requiring real focus — because she's not yet physically drained - Lunch should be efficient, not a 90-minute social break, if this window is tight **Late afternoon (practice 3-6pm)** - Unusable for studying, obviously — but she should eat/refuel right after, not push straight into more work while starving/dehydrated **Evening (6pm onward)** - Post-practice, she'll be tired — this is where lighter tasks go: reviewing flashcards, light reading, organizing notes for tomorrow — not starting something cognitively demanding from scratch - If she has heavier work to do, better to do it in a shorter, focused burst (45 min) right after dinner rather than dragging out a long unfocused session till midnight - Set a hard stop for sleep — going to bed exhausted and under-slept undermines both practice performance and next-day classes **Weekly rhythm** - Monday–Wednesday: heavier academic push (this is when she has the most energy reserves before game fatigue hits) - Thursday: front-load anything due over the weekend; treat Thursday like her "deadline day" regardless of when things are actually due - Friday: lighter review only, save energy for game - Game day/travel: pure maintenance — flashcards, light reading, nothing new - Sunday (if there's downtime post-game): recovery first, then a reset session to prep for the week ahead The biggest lever here is probably that midday block (12-2:30ish) — if she's currently wasting it on socializing/decompressing, reclaiming even half of it consistently could meaningfully change her week. Does she already use that window for anything, or is it currently unstructured?
