14:12:29 | INFO | 🤖 Target: Here's a game-week version, adjusted for travel disruption and the reality that Thu-Sun looks totally different from a normal week: --- **GAME WEEK TRACKER** | Day | Status | Study Block Happened? | Time Used (mins) | What I worked on | Notes | |-----|--------|------------------------|--------------------|--------------------|-------| | Mon | Normal | | | | | | Tue | Normal | | | | | | Wed | Normal | | | | | | Thu | Travel/Prep | | | | | | Fri | Travel/Away | | | | | | Sat | Game Day | | | | | | Sun | Recovery | | | | | **Pre-travel checklist (do this Wednesday night, not Thursday morning):** - [ ] Anything due Fri-Mon finished or nearly finished - [ ] Reading/materials downloaded or packed (don't rely on wifi during travel) - [ ] Flashcards or light-review material packed for bus/plane - [ ] Professors emailed if there's a conflict this week **During travel (Thu/Fri) — realistic goals only:** - [ ] Reviewed notes / flashcards (not new material) - [ ] Read assigned pages (if manageable) - [ ] Did NOT try to start anything requiring deep focus **Game day (Sat):** - No expectation of academic work — this is a maintenance-only day. Trying to force study time here usually backfires. **Recovery day (Sun):** - [ ] Slept in / recovered physically first - [ ] Light reset: reviewed what's due Mon/Tue - [ ] Planned Monday's schedule so the week starts organized, not scrambling **End of game-week check-in:** 1. Did I finish Thu-Mon work *before* Thursday? Y/N 2. What did I actually manage during travel? (be honest, not aspirational) 3. What's the first thing due Monday/Tuesday that needs attention? 4. Anything I need to email a professor about this week? --- **Key difference from the normal-week tracker:** the emphasis shifts from "did the block happen" to "was the prep done in advance." Game weeks aren't about finding new pockets of time — they're about front-loading Mon-Wed so Thu-Sun can be lower-pressure by design, rather than trying to squeeze in real studying during travel and games where it usually won't happen well anyway. Might be worth having her use the normal tracker for non-game weeks and this one for game weeks, so she's not forcing the same expectations onto very different weeks. Let me know if you want a condensed one-page version combining both for quick reference.
